The default estimator is an MM-estimator. See
\code{\link[robustbase:lmrob]{robustbase::lmrob()}} and
\code{\link[robustbase:lmrob.control]{robustbase::lmrob.control()}} for the
available estimators and their controls. The initial robust fit uses
random subsampling, so set the random seed to reproduce a fit.
}

\subsection{Preprocessing requirements}{

Factor/categorical predictors need to be converted to numeric values
(e.g., dummy or indicator variables) for this engine. When using the
formula method via \code{\link[=fit.model_spec]{fit()}}, parsnip will
convert factor columns to indicators.
}

\subsection{Case weights}{

This model can utilize case weights during model fitting. To use them,
see the documentation in \link{case_weights} and the examples
on \code{tidymodels.org}.

The \code{fit()} and \code{fit_xy()} functions have arguments called
\code{case_weights} that expect vectors of case weights.

Case weights are passed to the \code{weights} argument of
\code{\link[robustbase:lmrob]{robustbase::lmrob()}}. They are prior weights,
distinct from the robustness weights calculated by the estimator. See
the robustbase documentation for their interpretation.
}

