Confidence and prediction intervals use
\code{\link[robustbase:predict.lmrob]{robustbase::predict.lmrob()}} and its
covariance and scale estimates. The \code{level} argument to \code{predict()} sets
their nominal coverage. These intervals retain the assumptions of the
underlying method; robust estimation does not by itself guarantee
coverage under arbitrary contamination or heteroscedasticity.

Use \code{type = "raw"} with \code{opts} to pass prediction arguments directly to
\code{\link[robustbase:predict.lmrob]{robustbase::predict.lmrob()}}.
}

